  "articleBody": "Drywall tape bubbling is a common headache that can really mess up a smooth finish. One of the biggest reasons this happens is applying the joint compound too thickly underneath the tape. You want a thin, even layer to embed the tape into. Another frequent mistake is not embedding the tape firmly enough into that wet compound. If there's air trapped underneath, you're pretty much guaranteed bubbles. Rushing the drying time is another major no-no. Each coat needs to dry thoroughly, sometimes even overnight, before you apply the next one. Trying to speed this up can cause the compound to shrink unevenly, leading to those pesky bubbles or even cracks. Skipping pre-filling of joints, especially larger gaps, can also contribute to bubbling as the tape tries to bridge too much space. Lastly, using the wrong type of tape for the specific application or not using enough mud to properly feather the edges can also be factors. If you're finding yourself constantly battling bubbles, it might be worth getting some professional guidance. We can help you identify what's going wrong and ensure you get a smooth, bubble-free wall every time. Give us a call!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
